  "source_invariants": [
    "Core prospective_f64_matrix_ownership validates the actual plain-F64 schema, shape bounds and cardinality and computes complete canonical byte/node ownership. It constructs no payload, snapshot, import, permit or view.",
    "Finalized fresh F64 owners reuse the same constant-time cost calculation. The original canonical traversal remains for other data, nested roots and rebound metadata retaining an older shape owner. Current schema keys remain checked.",
    "Independent tests compare with the maintained generic traversal, actual same-budget imports, zero-sized and rank2/rank3 arrays, dynamic parameters, arbitrary F64 bits including infinities/NaNs/signedzero, rebound owners, wrong keys, type/bound/cardinality denial and overflow.",
    "All94 shared snapshot checks,6 region checks,24 matrix checks and30 original/decoded PolyBench correctness cases pass; both runtime-only and compiler feature builds pass.",
    "The source-region inventory is compiler-only while it has no runtime consumer; no unused prototype cache is retained in runtime-only metadata. Independent compiler/image paths rederive the inventory and diagnostics explicitly report selected:false. Remove these temporary feature gates when the admitted region execution path is integrated.",
    "No Mech port, input, C binary/flag, limit, tolerance, objective, split or timing-boundary change. No source fee is reduced and no scalar native capability is retired."
  ],
  "development_failures": [
    "The initial thin Core test command omitted functions required by existing bytecode tests; no source change was needed. The production feature closure passed all three targeted ownership tests.",
    "The first runtime-only feature check caught unused source-only prototype metadata. The inventory is compiler-gated until a real runtime loan consumes it; both standalone feature checks now pass. All failed commands/logs/source are retained."
  ],
